  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.2. Increased institutional capacity of workers&#x2019; organizations</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In January 2023, RAVAKSUR Trade Union Federation developed and submitted to the tripartite wage council their proposal concerning the need to change minimum wage setting. 

In April-June 2023, RAVAKSUR Trade Union Federation developed a trade union proposal on identifying short- and long-term challenges facing the pension system and in particular private pension funds. They came up with a set of proposals to be considered in the social security system reform. The ILO provided technical advice and organised a workshop in December 2022 on minimum wage setting.  Fifty participants from trade unions as well as other members of the National Wage Council attended this workshop.
In February to April 2023, the ILO supported research to assess the current state of the pension system in Suriname from a trade union perspective. In April 2023, the ILO supported a seminar where the report was presented and discussed and joint trade union position and proposal on pension system reform was formulated.</narrative>
   </description>
